TransformWheels: contiguous wheel world-position vector (scattered-locals class)

TransformWheels passes &local_24 (a 3-int wheel world position) to FUN_004203dc
per wheel; Ghidra split the block into three scalars, gcc scatters them -> the
transformed wheel positions were scrambled. Wheel positions feed Map_Height and
the car landing dynamics (Car_Landed reads the per-wheel heights @0x794c..),
which made identical-state landings produce different impulses and spark counts
(rand desync at L2 frame 0x88 tick 2: +3 native vs +18 wasm rand calls).

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
